.0},{\"vid\":\"K1WrHH-WtaA\",\"title\":\"Steve Jobs: Sale/Marketing People vs.  Product People\",\"channel\":\"Think Multiply\",\"summary\":\"A short clip of Steve Jobs explaining how sales and marketing people take over mature companies from product people, leading to product decline.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it whenever a company stagnates, from Intel to Boeing, to explain what happens when salespeople or finance run the business.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"product vs sales leadership\",\"categories\":[\"Management, leadership & organizations\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"Product, marketing & sales\"],\"tags\":[\"steve jobs\",\"company decline\",\"product management\",\"marketing\",\"management\"],\"quote\":\"I think this Steve Jobs clip explains it pretty well.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"K8kua5B5K3I\",\"title\":\"Inside a Secret Chinese Bitcoin Mine\",\"channel\":\"Motherboard\",\"summary\":\"Motherboard's 2014 visit to a secretive Bitcoin mining operation in a repurposed factory in Liaoning, China, one of six sites producing about 4,050 bitcoins a month. It shows the machines and the workers' living conditions.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN links it as a rare look inside a large Chinese mining operation, with its deafening machine noise and workers' conditions.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bitcoin mining\",\"categories\":[\"Cryptography\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\",\"Tech industry & business models\"],\"tags\":[\"bitcoin\",\"china\",\"mining farm\",\"motherboard\",\"cryptocurrency\"],\"quote\":\"The noise of these machines is incredibly loud and annoying even in the edited video\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"KAm7qAKAXwI\",\"title\":\"How anti-theft tags work - magnetostriction\",\"channel\":\"Applied Science\",\"summary\":\"Applied Science explains how retail anti-theft tags work. A tiny magnetostrictive strip acts as a mechanical oscillator excited by a magnetic field, and magnetizing or demagnetizing it arms or disarms the tag.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an informative explanation of what those tags are, especially in threads about implants and RFID.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"magnetostrictive anti-theft tags\",\"categories\":[\"Everyday physics & science demos\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"magnetostriction\",\"anti-theft tags\",\"physics\",\"eas\",\"applied science\"],\"quote\":\"here's an interesting and informative video from Applied Science on how these tags work\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"KBMU6l6GsdM\",\"title\":\"Missile defense multiple kill vehicle hover test\",\"channel\":\"theworacle\",\"summary\":\"Short US Missile Defense Agency footage of the December 2008 free-flight hover test of Lockheed Martin's Multiple Kill Vehicle. The test showed it hovering for 20 seconds while tracking a simulated target.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as striking evidence of long-standing kinetic interceptor and hover-control technology.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"missile defense\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Robotics\"],\"tags\":[\"kill vehicle\",\"lockheed martin\",\"interceptor\",\"hover test\",\"rocket control\"],\"quote\":\"the MKV thing is so rad\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"KCkbp4wurW0\",\"title\":\"Dark Castle (1986) - Original Macintosh Version!\",\"channel\":\"Classic Mac Gaming\",\"summary\":\"Gameplay footage of the original 1986 Macintosh version of Dark Castle by Silicon Beach Software. The uploader argues the original is a great game that was tarnished by inferior ports.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it to show a classic early Mac game, noting its low-latency input and early audio showcase.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"classic mac games\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\"],\"tags\":[\"dark castle\",\"macintosh\",\"retro gaming\",\"1980s\",\"silicon beach software\"],\"quote\":\"arguably the best non-educational game for the original Macintosh\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"KClAPipnKqw\",\"title\":\"Technical leadership and glue work - Tanya Reilly | #LeadDevNewYork\",\"channel\":\"LeadDev\",\"summary\":\"Tanya Reilly's LeadDev talk on glue work, the invisible coordination and support tasks engineers do that keep teams successful but can hurt careers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN refers to it in career and promotion discussions, including its warning about doing glue work too early in your career.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"glue work in engineering\",\"categories\":[\"Software practice, open source & careers\",\"Management, leadership & organizations\"],\"tags\":[\"glue work\",\"technical leadership\",\"career growth\",\"promotion\",\"engineering teams\"],\"quote\":\"Here is a talk which warns against doing this kind of glue work too early in your career\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"KRvv0QdruMQ\",\"title\":\"Are There Lost Alien Civilizations in Our Past?\",\"channel\":\"Kurzgesagt – In a Nutshell\",\"summary\":\"Kurzgesagt asks whether advanced civilizations could have existed on Earth in the deep past and left little evidence. It looks at time as a dimension for searching for alien civilizations and the limits of the geological record.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN brings it up in threads on ancient civilizations and detecting past technology in geology.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ancient civilizations and aliens\",\"categories\":[\"Geology & earth science\",\"Cosmology & astrophysics\"],\"tags\":[\"silurian hypothesis\",\"geological record\",\"fermi paradox\",\"kurzgesagt\"],\"quote\":\"I enjoyed Kurzgesagt's video [0] about our ability to sense ancient aliens.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0}",
    ",{\"vid\":\"KX_0c9R4Fng\",\"title\":\"DEF CON 23 - Marc Rogers and Kevin Mahaffey - How to Hack a Tesla Model S\",\"channel\":\"DEFCONConference\",\"summary\":\"A DEF CON 23 talk by Marc Rogers and Kevin Mahaffey walking through the architecture of the Tesla Model S, what Tesla got right and wrong, and how the interconnected systems can be hacked. It also covers the data the car collects.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as a detailed technical reference on Tesla's security design, especially the firewalling of infotainment from the CAN bus.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"automotive security\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\"],\"tags\":[\"tesla model s\",\"car hacking\",\"can bus\",\"def con\",\"embedded systems\"],\"quote\":\"the software architecture of the Tesla was light-years ahead of what Jeep\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"KZeIEiBrT_w\",\"title\":\"The Strange Math That Predicts (Almost) Anything\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"A Veritasium video on how a feud between Russian mathematicians led to Markov chains and the modern prediction algorithms built on them. It covers the history and the math behind them.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an excellent, detailed history of Markov chains, often in threads on Markov models and language models.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"markov chains\",\"categories\":[\"Probability & game theory\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"markov chains\",\"probability\",\"history of mathematics\",\"prediction\",\"veritasium\"],\"quote\":\"this excellent Veritasium video about Markov and his chains\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"KZokQov_aH0\",\"title\":\"The Witness - A Great Game That You Shouldn't Play\",\"channel\":\"Joseph Anderson\",\"summary\":\"Joseph Anderson's long critique of Jonathan Blow's puzzle game The Witness, covering its gameplay, its hundreds 