ine-minute rant against homeopathy, alternative medicine and woolly thinking. It is delivered as a fast, rhyming monologue built around an encounter at a dinner party.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters link it as a funny, quotable takedown of alternative medicine and cite its lines (such as 'alternative medicine that works is called medicine') in threads on homeopathy.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"alternative medicine skepticism\",\"categories\":[\"Religion, belief & skepticism\",\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\",\"Life sciences (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"homeopathy\",\"beat poem\",\"skepticism\",\"stand-up\",\"science vs pseudoscience\"],\"quote\":\"a rather hilarious 9 minute beat poem by Tim Minchin\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"KuG_CeEZV6w\",\"title\":\"Can you fold paper more than 7 times with hydraulic press\",\"channel\":\"Hydraulic Press Channel\",\"summary\":\"The Hydraulic Press Channel folds an A3 sheet of paper past the supposed seven-fold limit and then crushes it with a press. It is a short, quirky experiment.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked in paper folding threads as a fun demonstration and as the video that made the channel famous.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"paper folding limit\",\"categories\":[\"Everyday physics & science demos\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"hydraulic press\",\"paper folding\",\"experiment\",\"crushing\"],\"quote\":\"It was this paper folding video (and the guy's unapologetic Finnish accent) that launched Hydraulic Press Channel to fame.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"Kzpv47o80eg\",\"title\":\"日本の家作り（据え付け作業）Japan builds house in 1 day\",\"channel\":\"Rachel and Jun\",\"summary\":\"Rachel and Jun film Toyota Home Aichi installing a prefabricated house unit in Japan, with the assembly and roof waterproofing completed in about half a day.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in prefab and housing threads as proof that high-quality modular homes can be assembled on site in hours.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"japanese prefab housing\",\"categories\":[\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"Manufacturing & industrial processes\"],\"tags\":[\"prefab homes\",\"modular construction\",\"toyota home\",\"japan\",\"housing\"],\"quote\":\"assembling a modular home in Japan\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"L-s_3b5fRd8\",\"title\":\"Elon Musk and Kevin Rose\",\"channel\":\"Kevin Rose\",\"summary\":\"Kevin Rose interviews Elon Musk in 2012 about his companies PayPal, SpaceX and Tesla. It includes Musk's short explanation of reasoning from first principles versus by analogy.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN pointed people to it for the original interview and Musk's concise take on first-principles thinking.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"elon musk interview\",\"categories\":[\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"Startups & entrepreneurship\",\"Space exploration & spaceflight\"],\"tags\":[\"elon musk\",\"first principles\",\"spacex\",\"tesla\",\"kevin rose\"],\"quote\":\"Elon Musk has a cute and short explanation of \\\"reasoning from first principle\\\" vs. \\\"reasoning by analogy\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"L43-XE1uwWc\",\"title\":\"Mike Levin - Live ALife 2020 Keynote - Robot Cancer\",\"channel\":\"ALife 2020 Conference\",\"summary\":\"Michael Levin's keynote at the ALife 2020 conference, 'Robot Cancer', on how bioelectric signaling in embryogenesis and regeneration informs unconventional computing, cognition and the 'software of life'. He argues biology offers lessons for building adaptive machines.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN readers point to it as a companion to other Levin material on bioelectricity, goal-directedness in cells and cancer as a breakdown in cell communication.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"bioelectricity and morphogenesis\",\"categories\":[\"Biology & biotechnology\",\"Consciousness & cognition\"],\"tags\":[\"michael levin\",\"bioelectricity\",\"regeneration\",\"cancer\",\"artificial life\",\"cognition\"],\"quote\":\"here is a similar keynote lecture from the same person, but a bit more recent and with a few other very interesting notes\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"L6A1Lt0kvMA\",\"title\":\"Facebook Freebooting - Smarter Every Day 128\",\"channel\":\"SmarterEveryDay\",\"summary\":\"Destin Sandlin of Smarter Every Day explains 'Facebook freebooting', where Facebook users re-upload YouTubers' videos natively and the original creators lose views and revenue. He describes his own attempts to get Facebook to act.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as the first-hand account of video piracy on Facebook whenever the platform's treatment of creators comes up.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"facebook video piracy\",\"categories\":[\"Internet culture & memes\",\"Tech industry & business models\",\"Law, policing & justice\"],\"tags\":[\"freebooting\",\"facebook\",\"content creators\",\"copyright\",\"youtube\"],\"quote\":\"\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"LA-gNoxSLCE\",\"title\":\"dotScale 2015 - John Graham-Cumming - I got 10 trillion problems, but logging ain't one\",\"channel\":\"dotconferences\",\"summary\":\"John Graham-Cumming of Cloudflare talks at dotScale 2015 about handling roughly 10 trillion log lines a month. The talk touches on Cloudflare's hardware, its logging stack and its use of Lua in Nginx.\",\"why_hn\":\"Mostly cited as a source for details of Cloudflare's architecture, such as LuaJIT-based request inspection and request volumes.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"large-scale logging infrastructure\",\"categories\":[\"Cloud, DevOps & reliability\",\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Distributed systems\"],\"tags\":[\"cloudflare\",\"logging\",\"lua\",\"nginx\",\"infrastructure\"],\"quote\":\"I discover