    ",{\"vid\":\"RJVL80Gg3lA\",\"title\":\"Visualizing Data Using t-SNE\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"A Google Tech Talk by Laurens van der Maaten, co-creator of t-SNE, on visualizing high-dimensional data by mapping it to two dimensions. It explains how the technique works and how it compares with other visualization approaches.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people point to it as the canonical explanation from the method's author whenever t-SNE comes up.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"dimensionality reduction\",\"categories\":[\"Data visualization & information design\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\"],\"tags\":[\"t-sne\",\"data visualization\",\"machine learning\",\"high-dimensional data\",\"embeddings\"],\"quote\":\"there's a really interesting Google techtalk on how it works\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"RJh9yTIBY48\",\"title\":\"What salt tastes the best? Li, Na, K, Rb, Cs and more\",\"channel\":\"Explosions&Fire\",\"summary\":\"The Explosions&Fire channel taste-tests the chloride salts of the alkali metals (lithium through cesium), plus some alkaline earth metals and ammonium. The presenter describes the flavors, and the results are more pleasant than expected.\",\"why_hn\":\"It gets linked in threads about salt and taste as a quirky, memorable curiosity.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"salt taste chemistry\",\"categories\":[\"Chemistry\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"alkali metals\",\"taste test\",\"salts\",\"chemistry\",\"cesium\"],\"quote\":\"One of my favorite random youtube videos\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"RKXZ7t_RiOE\",\"title\":\"Pricing Design Work & Creativity (The Guide)\",\"channel\":\"The Futur\",\"summary\":\"The Futur's guide to pricing design and creative work, arguing against hourly rates and for value-based pricing. It features Blair Enns and says to price the client, not the job.\",\"why_hn\":