type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"developer infrastructure\",\"categories\":[\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\"],\"tags\":[\"facebook\",\"mercurial\",\"continuous integration\",\"monorepo\",\"developer productivity\"],\"quote\":\"It's a long video but it's very watchable using the YouTube speed multiplier.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"X36ye-1x_HQ\",\"title\":\"Type-Driven Development in Idris — Edwin Brady\",\"channel\":\"Scala World\",\"summary\":\"Edwin Brady, creator of Idris, introduces type-driven development in a dependently typed language. He shows types being written first and programs derived with interactive editing, then extends beyond simple examples to programs that interact with users and networks.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a demonstration of type-directed editing with typed holes, which some see as a likely future of programming.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"dependent types\",\"categories\":[\"Programming language design\",\"Functional programming\",\"Logic & formal methods\"],\"tags\":[\"idris\",\"type-driven development\",\"typed holes\",\"functional programming\",\"interactive editing\"],\"quote\":\"Something like that is likely the future of programming!\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"XCvwCcEP74Q\",\"title\":\"The Four Horsemen: Amazon/Apple/Facebook & Google - Who Wins/Loses (Scott Galloway, L2 Inc.) | DLD15\",\"channel\":\"DLD Conference\",\"summary\":\"Scott Galloway's DLD15 talk assessing the competitive positions of Amazon, Apple, Facebook and Google. He argues about where each is strong and weak, including Amazon's need for physical retail.\",\"why_hn\":\"Shared in 2015 threads as an insightful framework for strategic moves by the big tech companies.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"big tech strategy\",\"categories\":[\"Tech industry & busi