y\":\"A long Tsoding Daily programming stream in which he implements hot code reloading in C by loading a dynamic library at runtime without stopping the main program. It also touches on migrating struct versions across reloads.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it as a hands-on example of hot reloading and live coding in C.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"hot code reloading in c\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\",\"Operating systems & kernels\"],\"tags\":[\"c\",\"hot reload\",\"dynamic libraries\",\"live coding\",\"tsoding\"],\"quote\":\"he hot reloads a dynamic library without interrupting the main program, to test different functionality.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"YAPt_DcWAvw\",\"title\":\"Antique 4x5 camera creates 20 micron photolithography masks: Super tiny tax form\",\"channel\":\"Applied Science\",\"summary\":\"Ben Krasnow of Applied Science uses an antique 4x5 view camera to make high-resolution photolithography masks in a home shop. He photographs a poster-sized printout onto litho film to get features around 20 microns.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as an accessible way to make lithographic masks at home, in threads about hobbyist chip fabrication.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"home photolithography\",\"categories\":[\"Semiconductors & chip manufacturing\",\"Chemistry\"],\"tags\":[\"photolithography\",\"photomask\",\"ben krasnow\",\"view camera\",\"microfabrication\"],\"quote\":\"There is a great video on creating lithographic masks on Ben Krasnow's Applied Science channel\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0}",
    ",{\"vid\":\"YAneTFiz5WU\",\"title\":\"AR15: Mud Test\",\"channel\":\"InRangeTV\",\"summary\":\"InRangeTV subjects an AR-15 to a mud test in the same mud and location as a preceding AK-47 test. It shows how the rifle runs when covered in mud.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in AR versus AK reliability debates as evidence that the AR-15 handles mud better than its reputation suggests.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"rifle reliability\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"ar-15\",\"ak-47\",\"mud test\",\"firearms\",\"reliability\"],\"quote\":\"the purported advantages of AK action over its competitors in this regard are rather drastically overstated in popular culture\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"YE8MVNMzpbo\",\"title\":\"Killing the Walk Monster\",\"channel\":\"Molly Rocket\",\"summary\":\"Casey Muratori's remastered BICFest 2018 talk on how the collision system of The Witness was engineered to prevent whole classes of bugs found in game engines. It covers character movement and collision handling.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the explanation of how The Witness solved walking and collision.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"game collision systems\",\"categories\":[\"Game programming & engines\",\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"collision detection\",\"the witness\",\"casey muratori\",\"character movement\",\"game engines\"],\"quote\":\"talking about the problem and how they solved it in The Witness\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"YGIvWT-NBHk\",\"title\":\"Alen Ladavac - Taking CI and automated testing seriously - WebCamp Zagreb 2018\",\"channel\":\"WebCamp Zagreb\",\"summary\":\"Alen Ladavac of Croteam talks about continuous integration and automated testing pipelines in games, with case studies from The Talos Principle and Serious Sam.\",\"w