tal physics\"],\"tags\":[\"feynman\",\"babylonian mathematics\",\"axioms\",\"physics vs mathematics\",\"learning math\"],\"quote\":\"Feynman was an excellent communicator\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"YcVSgYz5SJ8\",\"title\":\"Sarah C. M. Paine — Why dictators keep making the same fatal mistake\",\"channel\":\"Dwarkesh Patel\",\"summary\":\"Dwarkesh Patel interviews Sarah Paine, a Naval War College historian, about continental versus maritime powers and how that explains decisions by Xi and Putin. They also cover a possible Taiwan war, the fall of the British Empire, WW2 strategy and how to study history.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters use it as a source for Paine's continental-versus-maritime framework and her views on sanctions when discussing geopolitics.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"geopolitical strategy and history\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Military history & warfare\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"sarah paine\",\"maritime power\",\"china\",\"russia\",\"military history\",\"sanctions\"],\"quote\":\"has some interesting ideas\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"YdtE3aIUhbU\",\"title\":\"TMS Bicycle, stable without gyros or trail (TMS=two-mass-skate)\",\"channel\":\"Arend Schwab\",\"summary\":\"Arend Schwab demonstrates a research bicycle, the two-mass-skate design, that balances itself without gyroscopic effects or trail. It challenges the common explanations for why a moving bicycle stays upright.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it as the author's own demonstration of research showing that bicycle stability is not explained by gyroscopes.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"bicycle dynamics\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"bicycle stability\",\"gyroscopic effect\",\"trail\",\"physics\",\"self-stability\"],\"quote\":\"Explanati