aking & video production\"],\"tags\":[\"commercial\",\"practical effects\",\"rube goldberg\",\"honda\",\"advertising\"],\"quote\":\"Rube Goldberg machine all done without CGI (5 months of pre-work, then 605 takes until they got to one that didn't screw up somewhere)\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"a3ww0gwEszo\",\"title\":\"Find the Longest Path\",\"channel\":\"switchbg\",\"summary\":\"Find the Longest Path is a comedic song by Daniel J. Barrett, a Billy Joel parody that describes the NP-hard longest path problem in informal terms.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN shares it as a fun, memorable way to explain the longest path problem and as an entry in lists of programming and math songs.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"longest path problem\",\"categories\":[\"Satire & parody\",\"Computability & complexity theory\",\"Algorithms & data structures\"],\"tags\":[\"longest path\",\"parody song\",\"complexity\",\"graph theory\",\"np-hard\"],\"quote\":\"you can listen to a Billy Joel parody that describes the problem in decidedly less academic terms\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"aFdpBqmDpzM\",\"title\":\"AWS re:Invent 2020: Working backwards: Amazon’s approach to innovation\",\"channel\":\"AWS Events\",\"summary\":\"An AWS re:Invent session explaining Amazon's Working Backwards process, where teams start from customer needs and write a press release and FAQ (PR-FAQ) before building. It covers the five customer questions that frame the process.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as the primary source for Amazon's Working Backwards method whenever product-definition approaches come up.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"product development process\",\"categories\":[\"Product, marketing & sales\",\"Tech company stories & documentaries\",\"Management, leadership & organizations\"],\"tags\":[\"working backwards\",\"pr-faq\",\"amazon\",\"innovation\",\"product management\"],\"quote\":\"A nice video\",