\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"US politics & elections\"],\"tags\":[\"putin\",\"russia\",\"julia ioffe\",\"frontline\",\"journalism\"],\"quote\":\"I can also recommend the PBS Frontline interviews with Julia Ioffe\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"b2mnbyRgXkY\",\"title\":\"XDC 2020 - Day 1 - September 16, 2020\",\"channel\":\"X.Org Foundation\",\"summary\":\"Day one of the X.Org Developer's Conference 2020 stream, including talks on the Raspberry Pi 4 Vulkan driver, the WSL graphics architecture, X11 and Wayland apps in WSL, and Mesa for D3D12.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked for the Microsoft talks on WSL GUI support and how WDDM drivers map into the Linux VM.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"linux graphics stack\",\"categories\":[\"Linux & open-source ecosystems\",\"Computer graphics & rendering\",\"Operating systems & kernels\"],\"tags\":[\"wsl\",\"wslg\",\"mesa\",\"d3d12\",\"xdc\"],\"quote\":\"If you're interested in the lowlevel WDDM driver <-> VM driver mapping, seek to 1:18:01\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"b6URa-PTqfA\",\"title\":\"1979: Will WORD PROCESSORS start a HOME WORKING revolution? | Past Predictions | BBC Archive\",\"channel\":\"BBC Archive\",\"summary\":\"A 1979 BBC Nationwide report asking whether word processors and networked microprocessors could end office commuting. It shows early word processing and a woman working from home, with surprisingly prophetic predictions.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN finds it a striking historical look at early text editors and remote work that feels very modern.\",\"content_type\":\"news\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of remote work\",\"categories\":[\"History of computing\",\"Labor, work & inequality\"],\"tags\":[\"bbc archive\",\"word processors\",\"1979\",\"working from home\",\"office computing\"],\"quote\":\"Perhaps it's better to see for a minute how people used this kind of editors when they first appeared\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"b9ifQvQCO7Y\",\"title\":\"Longhorn concept\",\"channel\":\"Arkmage2\",\"summary\":\"A concept video from 2003 showing an early vision of Windows Longhorn's interface, before it shipped as Vista.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited to contrast Microsoft's ambitious Longhorn vision with the Vista that actually shipped.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"windows longhorn concept\",\"categories\":[\"GUI, HCI & interface history\",\"UX & UI design\",\"Tech company stories & documentaries\"],\"tags\":[\"longhorn\",\"windows vista\",\"ui concept\",\"microsoft\"],\"quote\":\"Longhorn concept was awesome.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"bBx2Y5HhplI\",\"title\":\"Nick Hanauer on inequality\",\"channel\":\"WatchExtraVideo\",\"summary\":\"Nick Hanauer's short TED University talk on economic inequality, which was famously not posted on TED's main site at first. He argues that rich people are not the job creators.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in debates about taxes, job creation and wealth redistribution, and for the controversy around its release.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"economic inequality\",\"categories\":[\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"nick hanauer\",\"ted\",\"inequality\",\"taxes\",\"job creators\"],\"quote\":\"You really need to watch\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"bEOOYbscyTs\",\"title\":\"Clojure is Not Afraid of the GPU - Dragan Djuric\",\"channel\":\"ClojureTV\",\"summary\":\"Dragan Djuric presents Clojure libraries for GPU and numerical computing, including ClojureCL, ClojureCUDA and Neanderthal. He shows how a dynamic REPL workflow can be combined with low-level hardware acceleration for machine learning and data science.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as the talk by the author of Neanderthal and the Clojure GPU libraries, including comparisons against the JVM and CPU.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"le