rown estate\",\"cgp grey\"],\"quote\":\"CGP Grey did a video explaining the true cost of the monarchy.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"bj8hMtWeTUg\",\"title\":\"1 Month with the Xreal Air AR Glasses\",\"channel\":\"The Tech Chap\",\"summary\":\"A one-month review of the Xreal (formerly Nreal) Air AR glasses by The Tech Chap, covering unboxing, setup, what the display looks like, and how mixed reality differs from AR. It ends with the reviewer's overall thoughts. The video is sponsored.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as a concrete example of lightweight AR glasses that work as a monitor replacement, a more comfortable alternative to VR headsets.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ar glasses\",\"categories\":[\"VR, AR & spatial computing\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"xreal air\",\"nreal\",\"ar glasses\",\"product review\",\"monitor replacement\"],\"quote\":\"they look like a much better approach to a monitor replacement device\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"boB6qu5dcCw\",\"title\":\"Ion drive: The first flight\",\"channel\":\"nature video\",\"summary\":\"Nature video showing MIT researchers flying the first plane with no moving parts, powered by an ion drive that creates an ionic wind from high-powered electrodes. The 5m-wide craft flies across a sports hall.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked as a quick demonstration of the ion plane in threads about silent aircraft and flying cars.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"electroaerodynamic propulsion\",\"categories\":[\"Aviation & aerospace engineering\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"ion drive\",\"mit\",\"ionic wind\",\"silent drones\",\"aircraft\"],\"quote\":\"if you want to see how it works and see it flying here is a YouTube link\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"bq2_wSsDwkQ\",\"title\":\"Journalism: Last Week Tonight with John Oliver (HBO)\",\"channel\":\"LastWeekTonight\",\"summary\":\"A Last Week Tonight segment on the decline of the newspaper industry and what it means for journalism, including local reporting. It uses John Oliver's comedic commentary and references the film Spotlight.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it in discussions of news economics and repackaged reporting, though some commenters say they distrust Oliver as a source.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"newspaper industry decline\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Satire & parody\",\"Tech industry & business models\"],\"tags\":[\"journalism\",\"newspapers\",\"john oliver\",\"media economics\",\"local news\"],\"quote\":\"John Oliver had a great segment on this\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"bvlzZnhZhrc\",\"title\":\"Locksmith ripoffs: Hidden camera investigation (Marketplace)\",\"channel\":\"CBC News\",\"summary\":\"CBC Marketplace investigates locksmith scams in the Greater Toronto Area. It exposes networks of fake Google Maps listings and fake reviews, and uses hidden cameras to show how low quotes turn into overcharges.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as a concrete demonstration of how fake local business listings on Google Maps are used for scams.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"fake business listings and scams\",\"categories\":[\"Law, policing & justice\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\"],\"tags\":[\"google maps\",\"locksmith scams\",\"fake reviews\",\"hidden camera\",\"consumer fraud\"],\"quote\":\"This video has a demo of what is happening\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"bwhU9goCiaI\",\"title\":\"How Japan Learned Semiconductors\",\"channel\":\"Asianometry\",\"summary\":\"Asianometry traces the 30-year rise and peak of Japan's semiconductor industry from the 1950s to the 1980s, covering how a postwar country gained competence in an emerging technology.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as an excellent history of