y, surveillance & cybercrime\"],\"tags\":[\"the onion\",\"facebook\",\"cia\",\"privacy\",\"satire\"],\"quote\":\"I love this The Onion video\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"cvZjhWE-3zM\",\"title\":\"The Nuclear Salt Water Rocket - Possibly the Craziest Rocket Engine Ever Imagined.\",\"channel\":\"Scott Manley\",\"summary\":\"Scott Manley explains the nuclear salt water rocket, Robert Zubrin's concept of a rocket fueled by a rapid nuclear reaction in uranium salt dissolved in water. He covers its extraordinary performance and the dangers of managing it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the go-to accessible video whenever nuclear rocket engines come up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"nuclear rocket propulsion\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Nuclear power & fusion\"],\"tags\":[\"nuclear salt water rocket\",\"spaceflight\",\"propulsion\",\"scott manley\",\"zubrin\"],\"quote\":\"Scott Manley does a great video talking about nuclear rocket engines[2]\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"cwN983PnJoA\",\"title\":\"Your toothbrush is worn-out!\",\"channel\":\"Applied Science\",\"summary\":\"Ben Krasnow of Applied Science uses a scanning electron microscope to compare new and worn toothbrush bristles. He shows how the microscopic texturing wears down with use.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters link it for electron micrographs of fresh versus worn bristles when toothbrush wear comes up.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"toothbrush wear\",\"categories\":[\"Materials science\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"electron microscope\",\"toothbrush\",\"materials\",\"applied science\",\"microscopy\"],\"quote\":\"You can find electron microscope scans of fresh toothbrushes and worn ones in this[0] Applied Science YouTube video.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"d-ruFmgTpqA\",\"title\":\"Garmin Emergency Autoland Flight Trial\",\"channel\":\"AVweb\",\"summary\":\"AVweb's flight trial of Garmin's Emergency Autoland system, which flies a plane to a runway and lands it when the pilot cannot. It is part of Garmin's Autonomi automation on the G3000 avionics.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a concrete demo of emergency autoland when threads discuss pilot incapacitation and aviation automation.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"aviation autoland\",\"categories\":[\"Aviation & aerospace engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"garmin\",\"autoland\",\"avionics\",\"general aviation\",\"automation\"],\"quote\":\"The real-life demo is pretty impressive\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"d6Pcp944sRI\",\"title\":\"Making purple gold\",\"channel\":\"NileRed\",\"summary\":\"NileRed tries to make a ring from pure purple gold, a gold-aluminium intermetallic that is brittle and hard to work with. The 53-minute video follows the chemistry and many failed attempts before he produces a finished ring.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN mentions it as a fascinating example of chemistry persistence and as something people learned from, such as discovering purple gold exists.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"purple gold chemistry\",\"categories\":[\"Chemistry\",\"Materials science\"],\"tags\":[\"purple gold\",\"metallurgy\",\"chemistry\",\"nilered\",\"jewelry\"],\"quote\":\"There's a fascinating video of a fellow trying to make a ring out of Purple Gold.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"d8BcCLLX4N4\",\"title\":\"How to slow down a stock exchange\",\"channel\":\"Tom Scott\",\"summary\":\"Tom Scott visits IEX, a stock exchange that slows down trading with a long coil of fiber. The coil removes the speed advantage of high-frequency traders.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as a quick, visual explanation of IEX's deliberate latency and of artificial delay as a fairness tool.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"high-frequency trading\",\"categories\":[\"Tech industry & business models\",\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Investing & personal finance\"],\"tags\":[\"iex\",\"stock exchange\",\"latency\",\"fiber\",\"market fairness\"],\"quote\":\"Tom Scott did a nice video [1] on IEX's setup with 38 miles of fiber\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"d99_h30swtM\",\"title\":\"The moiré effect lights that guide ships home\",\"channel\":\"Tom Scott\",\"summary\":\"Tom Scott investigates moire-effect beacons, called Inogon leading marks, a Swedish invention from the 1980s that shows different patterns depending on the viewer's position. He visits one used to mark an undersea cable and tracks down its history.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked as the accessible explanation of how moire navigation lights work.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"moire navigation beacons\",\"categories\":[\"Ships, submarines & maritime\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"moire effect\",\"inogon\",\"navigation lights\",\"maritime\",\"tom scott\"],\"quote\":\"the one that Tom Scott visits here\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"dE-vOscpiNc\",\"title\":\"NASA | Earthrise: The 45th Anniversary\",\"channel\":\"NASA Goddard\",\"summary\":\"NASA Goddard recreates the Apollo 8 Earthrise moment using Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter data, narrated by Andrew Chaikin and synced with the astronauts' recorded conversation. It marks the flight's 45th anniversary.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked as a visualization of how the famous Earthrise photo was taken.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"apollo 8 earthrise\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\"],\"tags\":[\"apollo 8\",\"earthrise\",\"nasa\",\"lunar reconnaissance orbiter\",\"space history\"],\"quote\":\"Wikipedia links to a nice visualization on youtube of the moments when the photo was taken\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0}",
