 thread touches on naming versus actually understanding something.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"names versus knowledge\",\"categories\":[\"Education & learning\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"feynman\",\"understanding\",\"learning\",\"education\",\"nova\"],\"quote\":\"You can know the name of a bird in many different languages, but that tells you nothing about it.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"gg40RWiaHRY\",\"title\":\"I Tried Turning Games Into Text\",\"channel\":\"Acerola\",\"summary\":\"Acerola explores building a shader that turns games into ASCII art, walking through techniques such as brightness mapping and edge detection to see whether it looks good.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to as a nice overview of implementing ASCII rendering as a post-processing shader.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"ascii art shaders\",\"categories\":[\"Computer graphics & rendering\",\"Creative coding & generative art\"],\"tags\":[\"ascii rendering\",\"post-processing\",\"sobel filter\",\"shaders\",\"graphics programming\"],\"quote\":\"This video is a nice overview of implementing a variation of the style in a post-processing shader\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"ggdYts4muu0\",\"title\":\"Tesla Virtual Power Plant\",\"channel\":\"InfoQ\",\"summary\":\"A QCon London 2020 talk by Tesla engineers on the architecture of Tesla's Virtual Power Plant. It covers aggregating distributed batteries and solar with vertically integrated hardware and software across cloud and edge.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as a technical look at how Tesla's VPPs and Autobidder work as distributed systems.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"virtual power plants\",\"categories\":[\"Distributed systems\",\"Renewables, batteries & storage\",\"Cloud, DevOps & reliability\"],\"tags\":[\"tesla\",\"vpp\",\"distributed systems\",\"energy s