    ",{\"vid\":\"jErqdRE5zpQ\",\"title\":\"Canon Cat\",\"channel\":\"Storia Informatica\",\"summary\":\"A short Italian-language clip about the Canon Cat, a text-oriented personal computer from Canon designed by Jef Raskin, who started the Macintosh project. It shows the machine in use.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as a quick look at what using a Canon Cat was actually like, in threads on Raskin, command interfaces and early Macintosh history.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"Canon Cat computer\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"GUI, HCI & interface history\",\"History of computing\"],\"tags\":[\"canon cat\",\"jef raskin\",\"retro computing\",\"text editing\",\"user interfaces\"],\"quote\":\"a great demonstration of what it would be like to use one now\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"jNa3axo40qM\",\"title\":\"Emacs Rocks! Episode 13: multiple-cursors\",\"channel\":\"emacsrocks\",\"summary\":\"A four-minute Emacs Rocks screencast demonstrating the multiple-cursors package for Emacs. It shows how editing at many places at once can replace repetitive manual edits.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as the canonical demo of multiple cursors and of fluent, efficient Emacs editing.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"emacs editing\",\"categories\":[\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"emacs\",\"multiple cursors\",\"screencast\",\"text editing\",\"productivity\"],\"quote\":\"One of the better examples of the usefulness of multiple cursors is from Emacs Rocks\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"jWWGmiZs4JA\",\"title\":\"Pentagon officially released 'UFO' videos: BUSTED (Part 3)\",\"channel\":\"Thunderf00t\",\"summary\":\"Thunderf00t goes through the three UFO videos released by the Pentagon and offers mundane explanations for each. He treats the footage as sensor artifacts, parallax and camera effects rather than alien craft.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters use