h\",\"collective intelligence\",\"social learning\",\"anthropology\",\"culture\"],\"quote\":\"the secret of our success is in the connections between us\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"jbp3kdJZ1_A\",\"title\":\"Is Starlink A Secret Radar Constellation?\",\"channel\":\"Noise In Space\",\"summary\":\"A 105-minute technical deep dive from Noise In Space evaluating whether Starlink satellites could work as synthetic aperture radar. It covers SAR signal-to-noise, amplifiers, antennas, duplexing, phased array beamforming and simulations of V2 Mini and V3 satellites.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as a rigorous radio-engineering analysis of what radar capability Starlink could plausibly have.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"starlink radar capability\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Electronics & circuit design\",\"Information theory & signal processing\"],\"tags\":[\"starlink\",\"synthetic aperture radar\",\"phased arrays\",\"satellites\",\"rf engineering\"],\"quote\":\"Check out this video that goes into a very deep technical explanation\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"jcvd5JZkUXY\",\"title\":\"All Creative Work Is Derivative\",\"channel\":\"Question Copyright\",\"summary\":\"A two-minute animated minute meme by Nina Paley, photographed at the Metropolitan Museum, showing how all creative work builds on what came before. It is set to music from the Sita Sings the Blues soundtrack.\",\"why_hn\":\"Used in copyright and AI-code debates to argue that creativity is inherently derivative.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"copyright and creativity\",\"categories\":[\"Law, policing & justice\",\"Free speech, censorship & civil liberties\",\"Visual arts, photography & architecture\"],\"tags\":[\"copyright\",\"remix culture\",\"nina paley\",\"public domain\",\"animation\"],\"quote\":\"They made a nice music video to further spread the idea\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"jeRgFqbBM5E\",\"title\":\"Could The Universe Be Inside A Black Hole?\",\"channel\":\"PBS Space Time\",\"summary\":\"A PBS Space Time episode asking whether our universe could sit inside a black hole. It covers what physicists think happens inside black holes and the arguments for and against this idea.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to as a clear treatment of the universe-in-a-black-hole idea whenever black hole cosmology comes up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"black hole cosmology\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"black holes\",\"cosmology\",\"general relativity\",\"pbs space time\"],\"quote\":\"was a huge relief and interesting dive into the q\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"jeghGhVdt9s\",\"title\":\"[593] Gallium vs. Titalium - Abus Padlock Meets a Gruesome End\",\"channel\":\"LockPickingLawyer\",\"summary\":\"LockPickingLawyer shows what happens when liquid gallium is applied to an aluminum Abus padlock, which weakens and breaks the metal. It is a short demonstration of gallium's effect on aluminum.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it whenever gallium or liquid metal comes up, as a vivid demonstration of gallium destroying aluminum.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gallium attacking aluminum\",\"categories\":[\"Materials science\",\"Chemistry\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"gallium\",\"aluminum embrittlement\",\"padlock\",\"liquid metal\",\"lockpicking\"],\"quote\":\"you should watch his video where he breaks a lock by simply applying Gallium to a lock\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"jltnBOrCB7I\",\"title\":\"Milton Friedman justifies not recalling the ford pinto\",\"channel\":\"RepublicansSuckDlCK\",\"summary\":\"A clip of Milton Friedman answering an audience member about Ford's decision not to recall the Pinto, in which he defends weighing safety costs against benefits. The uploader's framing is strongly hostile to Friedman.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as an example of cost-benefit reasoning about product safety in threads on recalls, security spending and Boeing.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"cost-benefit of product safety\",\"categories\":[\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\",\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\",\"Philosophy & ethics\"],\"tags\":[\"milton friedman\",\"ford pinto\",\"recalls\",\"business ethics\",\"safety tradeoffs\"],\"quote\":\"There is an entertaining video of Milton Friedman discussing the same issues with an audience member\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"joMK1WZjP7g\",\"title\":\"Crash Test 1959 Chevrolet Bel Air VS. 2009 Chevrolet Malibu (Frontal Offset) IIHS 50th Anniversary\",\"channel\":\"firedemon101\",\"summary\":\"An IIHS crash test pitting a 1959 Chevrolet Bel Air against a 2009 Malibu in a frontal offset collision for the institute's 50th anniversary. The old car's occupant space collapses while the modern car's protects its driver.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters cite it as stark evidence that modern cars are far safer than older ones, countering nostalgia for 'built like they used to'.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"vehicle crash safety\",\"categories\":[\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"crash test\",\"iihs\",\"car safety\",\"bel air\",\"malibu\"],\"quote\":\"This 2009 vs. 1959 offset crash shows how much things have changed\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"jofycaXByTc\",\"title\":\"Hybrid Power Split Device. eCVT transmission.\",\"channel\":\"David Patience\",\"summary\":\"A short animated explanation of the power split device in Toyota-style hybrids, a planetary gearset that works as an eCVT. It shows how engine and motor power are combined.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people link it in hybrid versus EV debates as a clear view of how simple the hybrid driv