es on analog TV.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a clear explainer of how analog TV and CRTs actually work, and as the entry point to the author's wider TV series.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"analog television\",\"categories\":[\"Audio & video engineering\",\"Electronics & circuit design\"],\"tags\":[\"crt\",\"ntsc\",\"pal\",\"scanlines\",\"broadcast tv\"],\"quote\":\"He actually demonstrates how the beam is redirected by the electro-magnets wrapped around the base of the tube. It's very cool.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"lBfVxBj61z0\",\"title\":\"Jellyvision Q&A with DHH & Jason Fried\",\"channel\":\"JellyvisionLab\",\"summary\":\"Jellyvision hosts Basecamp founders Jason Fried and David Heinemeier Hansson for a Q&A about open source, productivity, feature requests and taking care of customers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as an example of the founders' realistic, down-to-earth approach and their bootstrapped, lifestyle-business philosophy.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bootstrapped software business philosophy\",\"categories\":[\"Startups & entrepreneurship\",\"Hacker culture & free software\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\"],\"tags\":[\"dhh\",\"jason fried\",\"basecamp\",\"open source\",\"bootstrapping\"],\"quote\":\"he approaches things in a much more realistic down to earth manner than many other engineers out there.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"lGEMwh32soc\",\"title\":\"React without memo\",\"channel\":\"React Conf\",\"summary\":\"A React Conf talk by Xuan Huang previewing React Forget, a compiler that automatically memoizes components. It argues for making memoization the default so developers need not write useMemo or useCallback by hand.\",\"why_hn\":\"Shared in discussions of useCallback and memoization as the first look at where React was heading with an auto-memoizing compiler.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"leve