nda\"],\"quote\":\"I'm not saying you're self-censoring; I'm sure you believe everything you're saying.\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"lR0nh-TdpVg\",\"title\":\"The Memory Sinkhole - Unleashing An X86 Design Flaw Allowing Universal Privilege Escalation\",\"channel\":\"Black Hat\",\"summary\":\"Christopher Domas's Black Hat 2015 talk on a long-unnoticed x86 design flaw that lets an attacker reach System Management Mode, a ring below the OS. It explains how the legacy architecture allows universal privilege escalation and persistent, hard-to-detect malware.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in discussions of CPU hidden features, Intel's security failures and SMM malware as a concrete example of a forgotten processor feature being exploited.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"x86 system management mode exploits\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Computer architecture & CPUs\"],\"tags\":[\"x86\",\"smm\",\"privilege escalation\",\"black hat\",\"firmware security\",\"ring -2\"],\"quote\":\"There was a blackhat talk on embedding malware in SMM and triggering it with a magic number written to a register\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":1.0},{\"vid\":\"lRndE7rSXiI\",\"title\":\"seL4 Is Free – What Does This Mean For You?\",\"channel\":\"Linux.conf.au 2015 -- Auckland, New Zealand\",\"summary\":\"Gernot Heiser presents seL4, a microkernel with a mathematical proof connecting security properties to the binary code, and explains what its open-sourcing means for users. It covers its roles as a microkernel, separation kernel and hypervisor.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited to explain what formal verification of seL4 guarantees, such as ruling out whole classes of bugs like buffer overflows.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"formally verified operating systems\",\"categories\":[\"Operating systems & kernels\",\"Logic & formal methods\",\"Security & hacking\"],\"tags\":[\"sel4\",\"microkernel\",\"formal verif